@startmindmap exp4_map
title Experiment 4 - map: every strategy, uncontended and contended, one run
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

* Exp 4: all strategies in one run
** Question
*** What does each strategy cost alone, and what does it cost when a second thread joins?
** Setup
*** Uncontended: 1 thread on CPU 2, 20 M increments
*** Contended: 2 threads on CPUs 2 and 4, 5 M increments each
*** Order of strategies rotates every trial
** Uncontended results, ns per increment
*** plain reference: 0.20 (only correct with one thread)
*** fetch_add: 1.34
*** CAS loop: 1.72
*** spinlock: 1.53
*** mutex: 4.15
** Contended results, ns per increment, slowest thread
*** fetch_add: 8.23
*** CAS loop: 21.69, about 0.6 failed attempts per increment
*** spinlock: 23.28
*** mutex: 25.76, 36.5 percent kernel time
** Lesson
*** The uncontended cost is small; the contended cost is what matters
*** fetch_add is the cheapest correct option at both levels
** Concepts to read first
*** Concept 05: spinlock
*** Concept 06: fetch_add vs CAS
@endmindmap
